        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"C3\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V LDO may oscillate / be unstable, so the +5V rail feeding the MCUs (U1.8, U2.8), the potentiometer (J9.1) and the reset pull-up (R8.1) could be noisy or out of regulation, causing erratic operation or resets.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Connectivity, component types, polarities and footprints all check out against standard practice, but the LM1117-5.0's output capacitor (C3) is only 100nF instead of the ~10µF the regulator needs for stability, so the +5V rail may be unstable."
}

